# flight GitHub test rig — copy to test-rig/github/.env (gitignored) and fill in.
# The rig targets the real repo hardcoded in up.sh (OWNER/REPO); only the token comes from here.
# Alternatively export FLIGHT_GH_TOKEN in your shell — the env var wins over this file.

# Token: fine-grained PAT restricted to the test repo (or classic PAT).
# Minimum scopes: repo + workflow (classic), or for fine-grained: Contents, Issues,
# Pull requests, Actions, Workflows — read & write. Full list: flight/references/backends.md.
FLIGHT_GH_TOKEN=ghp_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
